{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Accessibilities Committee | Area 75{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<div class="page-title-bar">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="{{ path('app_home') }}">Home</a> › <a href="#">Area Business</a> › <span>Accessibilities</span></div>
    <h1>Accessibilities</h1>
    <p>Removing Barriers to the AA Message</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="page-content">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">

    <div class="panel" style="background:var(--cream-dark);">
      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <address style="font-style:normal;">
        <strong>Area 75 Accessibilities Chair — Amy V.</strong><br>
        📞 (414) 436-5282 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <a href="mailto:accessibilities@area75.org">accessibilities@area75.org</a>
      </address>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <p>The purpose of the Area 75 Accessibilities Committee is to assist AA members to find solutions to ensure that every alcoholic can participate in A.A. meetings, twelfth step work, and A.A. service.</p>
      <p>Our goal is to problem solve ways to carry the message of Alcoholics Anonymous to ALL alcoholics who reach out for it. This includes removing barriers — mental, physical, geographical, cultural, emotional, and technical — whether seen or unseen.</p>
      <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid var(--terracotta); padding:1rem 1.5rem; margin:1.5rem 0; font-style:italic; font-family:var(--font-serif); color:var(--brown-rich); font-size:1.05rem;">
        "I am responsible. When anyone, anywhere, reaches out for help, I want the hand of A.A. always to be there. And for that: I am responsible."
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Resources</h2>
      <ul class="pdf-link-list">
        <li><a href="/pdfs/self_assessment_guide" target="_blank">AA Accessibility Self Assessment Guide (Area 75)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.aa.org/assets/en_US/special-needs-accessibilities-committees/m-48i-special-needsaccessibilities-workbook" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Accessibilities Workbook</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.aa.org/aa-guidelines-accessibility-all-alcoholics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A.A. Guidelines on Accessibility for All Alcoholics</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.aa.org/assets/en_US/p-22_AAfortheOlderAA.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AA for the Older Alcoholic</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.aa.org/assets/en_US/mg-13_carryingtheaa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sharing the AA Message with the Alcoholic Who is Deaf</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://aa-intergroup.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AA Intergroup Online Meetings</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://sites.google.com/view/deafaa/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Deaf-AA Meetings</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
